                    briefing_title_r1:      `Round 1 — Diagnose the resilience gap`,
                    briefing_text_r1:       `It is the first day of the resilience cycle. Meridian earns <strong>A$96M</strong> at an 18% margin, but <strong>74% of revenue sits in one line — Sector Reports</strong> — renewal has slipped from 92% to <strong>86%</strong>, and a A$4.1M federal client just cancelled, citing a free generative-AI alternative. Compute the baseline resilience score and locate where the business is most brittle: <em>stream</em>, <em>client</em> or <em>vertical</em> concentration. Then separate the genuinely defensible asset — the <em>proprietary 30-year, 28-vertical datasets</em> — from the commoditising one — the repackaged public data the AI is already eating. Frame the A$12M against the Three Horizons of growth.`,
                    briefing_title_r2:      `Round 2 — Design and fund the new revenue streams`,
                    briefing_text_r2:       `Spend the A$12M to build diversification. The menu of five: a <strong>live analytics API</strong> (to meet DataLive head-on), a <strong>benchmarking SaaS</strong> tool, <strong>advisory</strong> services on the data, a <strong>data-licensing</strong> business, and an <strong>AI assistant</strong> built on your proprietary data moat. Each has an investment cost, a time-to-first-revenue, a margin profile and a cannibalisation risk against the flagship. Build a <em>portfolio, not a single bet</em> — and decide your position on cannibalising Sector Reports: refuse and you leave that revenue for DataLive and the free tools, or do it deliberately, on your own terms. The budget is fixed; Rounds 3 and 4 still need funding.`,
                    briefing_title_r3:      `Round 3 — Fund the explorative process pattern`,
                    briefing_text_r3:       `Escalation: two more clients (<strong>A$5.6M combined</strong>) just threatened to pilot DataLive. Products answer today — but what produces <em>product four</em> when the next disruption hits in 2028? Building on Rosemann's explorative-process work, fund <em>how</em> Meridian keeps creating value: an opportunity-sensing <strong>signals</strong> function, a stage-gated <strong>venture pipeline</strong>, or a <strong>data-product factory</strong> that industrialises new offerings. Set the operating cadence and leading indicators — and govern <em>explore separately from exploit</em>, so the core's 18% margin and quarterly targets don't strangle the ventures in month four.`,
