                    coach_default:          `Decision logged.`,
                    coach_r1_stream:        `<strong>That's the right read.</strong> The brittleness isn't the lost client or the renewal slip — those are symptoms. It's that <em>74% of revenue sits in one line</em> a free AI tool is already eating. Fix the concentration and the rest follows; chase the symptom and you'll be back here next quarter.`,
                    coach_r1_client:        `<strong>Client concentration is real, but it's the second-order problem.</strong> Win replacement logos for Sector Reports and you've just refilled the same brittle 74% stream. The structural risk is the stream itself, not which names sit inside it.`,
                    coach_r1_renewal:       `<strong>“Fix churn and the rest takes care of itself” treats the symptom.</strong> The renewal slip is the flagship's first material churn ever — a warning that the whole 74% stream is exposed. Defend renewals all you like; you're still a single-stream company a disruptor is pricing at one-third.`,
                    coach_r1_none:          `<strong>“A one-off, not a pattern” is exactly how this ends in a trade sale.</strong> The board paper is blunt: this is the leading edge. A 15% erosion of the flagship — plausible in 24 months — halves your EBIT. Underestimate it now and you'll be diagnosing it from the exit.`,
