                    coach_r1_sharp:         `<strong>Sharp diagnosis.</strong> You named stream concentration as the structural risk, separated the defensible 30-year dataset from the commoditising repackaging, and framed the A$12M across all three horizons. That's the resilience lens — now build the portfolio it points to.`,
                    coach_r2_portfolio:     `<strong>That's portfolio thinking.</strong> API to meet DataLive, benchmarking SaaS, and data-licensing — three streams with staggered timing and different risk profiles, so no single failure sinks the plan. Dependence falls, exposure drops, and new revenue starts to compound. This is diversification, not a replacement bet.`,
                    coach_r2_onterms:       `<strong>Cannibalising on your own terms is the right call.</strong> The AI assistant built on your proprietary moat will eat some of Sector Reports — but better you do it than DataLive and the free tools. You've turned the threat into a stream you own, and the question stopped being “whether” and became “on whose terms.”`,
                    coach_r2_cashcow:       `<strong>You've spent the budget making the brittle thing shinier.</strong> Seventy-four percent of revenue still sits in one stream a free AI tool is eating — your biggest client just proved it. A nicer Sector Reports is still one stream. Where is the second stream that survives if the flagship falls 15%? This is the error the whole cycle is meant to break.`,
                    coach_r2_single:        `<strong>One analytics API as the entire answer just swaps one concentration for another.</strong> If it's late, mispriced, or DataLive out-executes you, you've recreated the single-stream risk you were sent to fix. Resilience is a portfolio — where are your second and third streams, and how do their timings differ?`,
                    coach_r2_scatter:       `<strong>Five streams funded thinly is its own trap.</strong> None reaches escape velocity, every team is under-resourced, and you can't tell a winner from a straggler. A portfolio isn't “everything” — it's two or three streams funded enough to actually reach first revenue.`,
                    coach_r2_refuse:        `<strong>Refusing to build the AI assistant doesn't protect Sector Reports — it hands that revenue to DataLive.</strong> The cash cow gets cannibalised either way; the only choice is whether you do it on your terms or theirs. Protect it at all costs and you'll watch the free tools eat it for free.`,
                    coach_r2_ignore:        `<strong>Calling the AI assistant a distraction ignores the exact threat that started this.</strong> A free AI summary is why your largest client left. The assistant built on your proprietary data is how you answer it — sidelining it leaves the disruption unaddressed at its source.`,
