                    coach_r4_multi:         `<strong>A multi-pronged hedge is the mature move.</strong> An AI partnership, multi-year flagship lock-ins, and vertical expansion together cap the downside you can't out-build. You've accepted that not all disruption is solvable by innovation — and insured the part that isn't.`,
                    coach_r4_resilience:    `<strong>That's the pitch a board trusts.</strong> Dependence below 60%, a diversified portfolio, a repeatable explore engine, and hedges on the residual exposure — resilience as a designed outcome, not a decorated cash cow. The four KPIs back the story.`,
                    coach_r4_nohedge:       `<strong>“We'll out-innovate AI on every front” is a plan with no insurance.</strong> Maybe you will — but if you're wrong on even one stream, what's the backstop? Resilient firms hedge the downside they can't out-build. Calling insurance a sign of defeat is how the plan unravels on a single miss.`,
                    coach_r4_dump:          `<strong>Winding the flagship down fast is reckless.</strong> The cash cow still funds the whole transition — kill it before the new streams can carry the firm and you collapse the revenue and the valuation in one move. Milk it deliberately and lock it in; don't torch it.`,
                    coach_r4_decorate:      `<strong>“We modernised the flagship” is the board's least favourite sentence.</strong> They asked you to reduce single-stream dependence below 60% — a shinier Sector Reports doesn't move that number. Lead with resilience, or the chair pursues the trade sale you were hired to avoid.`,
